IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org
 /wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Elizabeth-Acevedo-Courtesy-of-the-Author-for-w
 ebsite.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/06/Elizabeth-Acevedo-Courtesy-of-the-Author-for-website.jpg
UID:7FoezLytm5QvoNXCFjKIv
SUMMARY:Inprint Cool Brains! Series presents Elizabeth Acevedo
DTSTAMP:20260810T100230Z
DTSTART:20261018T140000Z
DESCRIPTION: \n\nFree and open to the public\nFree copies of Anger Is Only 
	a Shadow for the first 100 families\nAppearance by celebrated Houston writ
	er Jasminne Mendez\nMeet the author followed by a book sale and signing\nB
	us scholarships available for student groups – full scholarships for publi
	c schools\, partial scholarships for private schools upon availability. Fo
	r information\, email info@inprint.org\n\nBooks available through Kindred 
	Stories\n\n\nAnd more!\n\n\nThe 2026/2027 Inprint Cool Brains! Series prou
	dly presents National Book Award winner and renowned poet Elizabeth Aceved
	o\, sharing her new YA novel Anger Is Only a Shadow. \nKnown for YA novels
	 filled with poetry\, humor\, and heart\, Elizabeth Acevedo is the New Yor
	k Times-bestselling author of The Poet X\, which won the National Book Awa
	rd for Young People’s Literature\, the Michael L. Printz Award\, the Pura 
	Belpré Award\, the Carnegie medal\, the Boston Globe–Horn Book Award\, and
	 the Walter Award. She is also the author of With the Fire on High\, which
	 was named a best book of the year by the New York Public Library\, NPR\, 
	Publishers Weekly\, and School Library Journal\; and Clap When You Land\, 
	which was a Boston Globe–Horn Book Honor book and a Kirkus finalist. Aceve
	do is a National Poetry Slam Champion and served as the 2022 Young People’
	s Poet Laureate. \n“An irresistible story of family connection\, resilienc
	e\, and loyalty” (Kirkus starred review)\, Anger Is Only a Shadow is Aceve
	do’s powerful new YA novel in prose and poetry. Lil is anything but small.
	 She’s rebellious\, she’s loyal\; she’s figuring out what kind of good per
	son she wants to be\, or if she wants to be a good person at all. But more
	 than anything? Lil wants to be free. When her instinct for freedom leads 
	to another stay in D.C. juvenile detention\, Lil knows she’s lucky to just
	 be on probation. But judgment\, guilt\, and an ankle monitor weigh heavil
	y on her\, and she can’t shake that pinned-down feeling. The only person w
	ho might understand is her big brother\, Aldwin. Except he’s more distant 
	now than just the hundred miles from his college. As her court hearing tic
	ks closer\, a question looms over Lil as the missed phone calls and strang
	e texts from her brother pile up: will she stay put\, or put her future fr
	eedom on the line? “A striking and nuanced portrait of the realities of ju
	venile detention and mental illness” (Publisher’s Weekly starred review) a
	nd “intensely genuine” (The Bulletin of the Center for Children’s Books st
	arred review)\, Anger Is Only a Shadow a white-knuckle journal to self-und
	erstanding and doing the right thing\, no matter the cost. \n\n\nhttps://i
	nprinthouston.org/event/inprint-cool-brains-series-presents-elizabeth-acev
	edo/\n\nFrom Inprint Houston
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-cool-brains-series-presents-el
	izabeth-acevedo/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
